Diagnostic: env-gated per-layer paint/invalidation logging (WEBKIT_PAINT_LOG=1).

Temporary instrumentation for the load-time paint-storm hunt: the
no-full-repaint-on-layer-grow patch removed the layer-resize invalidations
(verified with breakpoints: the setSize chain is gone) but franceinfo.fr
paint volume did not move (~600 paints / ~600 Mpx per load, A/B vs the
WEBKIT_REPAINT_ON_LAYER_RESIZE=1 kill-switch), so whole-layer paints are
reaching the tiled backing store through a path invalidation breakpoints
cannot attribute (inlining defeats gdb caller attribution; the dominant
"caller" turned out to be no-op setPaintingPhase({}) calls on brand-new
non-drawing clipping layers).

With WEBKIT_PAINT_LOG=1 (off by default, zero overhead when unset):
 - GLC FULL/RECT: every whole-layer damage and every >0.5 Mpx rect damage,
   with layer pointer + size (WebProcess stderr)
 - proxy INVAL: dirty rects arriving at each backing store proxy
 - proxy PAINT: every tile-paint pass (dirty tile count, union, contents
   size, tiles created)
 - proxy DROP-ALL: full tile drops with the reason bits
   (tileSizeChanged / contentsScaleChanged)

Correlating GLC/INVAL lines with PAINT lines over one franceinfo load
pinpoints which layer eats the ~200 screenfuls and which code path damages
it. Remove once the storm is fixed.

